 "geometry_notes": [
  "All outline dimensions transcribed from Şekil 3.1–3.3 (PDF pp 20–22, 200 dpi renders read visually); web height = H − 45 cm as printed.",
  "TİP I and TİP II: transcribed chain closes (10+12.5+4+18.5 = 45; 10+12.5+7.5+15 = 45) and reproduces the published F, yalt and Ix of Tablo 3.1/3.3 exactly (to the printed rounding).",
  "TİP III: the printed vertical chain 9.5+13.5+7.5+15 = 45.5 does not close with the printed web height H−45. With 13.5 the area is +13.75 cm² (+0.3–0.4%) over Tablo 3.5. Using a 13.0 cm top-splay height (chain closes to 45) reproduces F, yalt and Ix of Tablo 3.5 exactly for all three heights, so 13.0 is adopted (convention; the 13.5 label is taken as a drawing slip). Hence provenance 'transcribed-with-convention' for TİP III.",
  "TİP III top flange: 95 cm wide, 9.5 cm thick; the splay starts 10 cm in from each flange tip (the '10' callouts) and runs 27.5 cm horizontally to the 20 cm web.",
  "Sharp corners throughout (none drawn). Composite section = precast + 25 cm slab of transformed width b = 63.69 cm (TİP I/II) or 80.83 cm (TİP III) (n = 29440/36057); tests reproduce Tablo 3.2/3.4/3.6.",
  "Concrete C45 for precast beams, C30 for slab (§2.2)."
 ],
 "residuals": "Precast F, yalt, Ix: all 9 sizes match published values to printed rounding (|ΔF| ≤ 0.01 cm², |Δyalt| ≤ 0.005 cm, |ΔIx|/Ix < 1e-6) with the TİP III 13.0 cm splay convention. Composite Fc/ycalt/Icx reproduced within rounding (see tests)."
